WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:02.800
This is what a lot of drafts look like.

00:02.960 --> 00:06.000
Three versions of a word, split by slashes.

00:06.240 --> 00:07.600
A sentence written twice,

00:07.600 --> 00:09.040
because you couldn't decide.

00:09.360 --> 00:11.440
And at the bottom, everything you cut

00:11.440 --> 00:13.120
but couldn't bring yourself to delete.

00:13.835 --> 00:15.915
All of that deserves a better place.

00:17.022 --> 00:19.342
Vikalp is a plugin for Obsidian.

00:19.422 --> 00:21.582
The name is Hindi for alternative.

00:24.077 --> 00:26.077
Here's the same draft with Vikalp.

00:26.477 --> 00:28.317
A thin underline and a few dots

00:28.317 --> 00:29.597
mean there are other versions.

00:30.312 --> 00:32.392
Hover over it and use the arrow keys,

00:32.392 --> 00:34.632
and you read each one right where it lives.

00:35.112 --> 00:36.632
There's no accept button.

00:36.632 --> 00:38.312
Whatever's showing is the note.

00:38.792 --> 00:40.712
It works for whole sentences too.

00:41.352 --> 00:42.872
And it handles the small stuff.

00:43.032 --> 00:45.847
Swap pencil for eraser, and the article in

00:45.847 --> 00:48.967
front fixes itself, so it reads an eraser.

00:50.760 --> 00:52.840
To add your own, put the cursor on a word,

00:52.840 --> 00:54.360
and press Command J.

00:54.600 --> 00:56.440
Type the other ways you might say it,

00:56.440 --> 00:57.800
and try each one in the sentence.

00:58.545 --> 01:00.385
Press it again, and you're trying

01:00.385 --> 01:01.985
versions of the whole sentence.

01:02.465 --> 01:04.625
Once more, and it's the whole paragraph.

01:06.134 --> 01:08.534
This aside about lighthouses is nice,

01:08.534 --> 01:09.894
but it might not belong.

01:10.134 --> 01:12.329
Instead of deleting it, ghost it.

01:12.489 --> 01:14.409
It stays right there, faded,

01:14.489 --> 01:16.169
and it's left out of the word count.

01:16.409 --> 01:17.929
Bring it back whenever you want.

01:18.951 --> 01:21.351
This line is really a different essay,

01:21.351 --> 01:22.791
so it goes to Overflow.

01:23.111 --> 01:24.951
Cuts that used to pile up at the bottom of

01:24.951 --> 01:27.351
the page live here now, one Overflow per note.

01:27.826 --> 01:30.386
When one fits again, drag it back in.

01:31.818 --> 01:32.938
Stuck on a word?

01:33.018 --> 01:35.738
Type two question marks, and AI adds a few more.

01:36.948 --> 01:38.468
Each one gets a little robot,

01:38.468 --> 01:40.388
so you always know which words are yours.

01:40.468 --> 01:42.388
It never changes the note on its own.

01:42.708 --> 01:43.828
It just gives you options.

01:44.716 --> 01:47.436
When a draft feels done, run the linter.

01:47.436 --> 01:48.236
It

01:49.358 --> 01:51.918
It catches the usual habits: hedging,

01:51.998 --> 01:54.798
filler, sentences that go on too long.

01:54.958 --> 01:56.558
You can write your own rules too.

01:57.485 --> 01:58.605
There's even one for when you

01:58.605 --> 01:59.885
start sounding like LinkedIn.

02:01.656 --> 02:04.776
Then there's the Lab, a few passes for editing.

02:04.936 --> 02:07.976
It can catch typos, mark the weakest sentences,

02:08.057 --> 02:11.336
the ones that run long, or words that don't fit the tone.

02:11.656 --> 02:12.856
Or ask it to tighten things

02:12.856 --> 02:14.057
up by about twenty percent.

02:15.979 --> 02:17.819
It doesn't rewrite a single sentence.

02:17.819 --> 02:18.859
It only strikes out the

02:18.859 --> 02:20.379
words it thinks you can lose.

02:20.459 --> 02:21.979
If it cuts something you'd keep,

02:21.979 --> 02:23.339
click it, and it stays.

02:23.659 --> 02:26.379
Then ghost the cuts, so nothing is gone for good.

02:27.324 --> 02:28.204
Then hide everything,

02:28.204 --> 02:29.964
and read it the way a reader would.

02:33.551 --> 02:35.471
The AI never writes for you.

02:35.471 --> 02:37.630
It only helps you look at your own words,

02:37.630 --> 02:39.071
and only when you ask.

02:39.311 --> 02:41.471
And the note itself stays plain markdown.

02:41.790 --> 02:43.311
That's Vikalp.

02:43.311 --> 02:45.391
A writing plugin built for how you think.
